the target language is: lps.

% Multi-party obligations: buyer, seller and an escrow agent.
% Source: legacy_lps1/examples/CLOUT_workshop/Escrow.pl
% Covers: several events, guarded causal laws, the "to a time" suffix on an
% event that has already been observed (§3.1).

the maximum time is 10.

the events are:
    *a buyer* opens an escrow with *a seller* for *a value*; known as create_escrow.
    *a buyer* deposits *a value*; known as deposit.
    *a buyer* receives the goods; known as received_goods.
    *a buyer* accepts the goods; known as accept_goods.
    *a buyer* rejects the goods; known as reject_goods.

the actions are:
    shipping is authorised; known as authorise_shipping.
    *a party* is paid *a value*; known as pay.

the fluents are:
    *a buyer* has an escrow with *a seller* for *a value*; known as escrow.
    the balance of *an entity* is *a value*; known as balance.

the knowledge base escrow includes:

when a buyer opens an escrow with a seller for a value
    and it is not the case that a second buyer has an escrow with a second seller for a second value
then the buyer has an escrow with the seller for the value.

when a buyer deposits a value
    and the buyer has an escrow with a seller for the value
then the balance of the buyer is the value.

it must not be true that
    a buyer deposits a value from a first time to a second time
    and the balance of the buyer is a second value at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a buyer deposits a value from a first time to a second time
    and a second buyer has an escrow with a seller for a second value at the first time
    and the buyer is different from the second buyer.

it must not be true that
    a buyer deposits a value from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the buyer has an escrow with a seller for a second value at the first time.

if a buyer deposits a value from a first time to a second time
then shipping is authorised from the second time to a third time.

if a buyer receives the goods from a first time to a second time
    and the buyer accepts the goods to a third time
    and the buyer has an escrow with a seller for a value at the third time
then the seller is paid the value from the third time to a fourth time.

if a buyer receives the goods from a first time to a second time
    and the buyer rejects the goods to a third time
    and the buyer has an escrow with a seller for a value at the third time
then the buyer is paid the value from the third time to a fourth time.

when a party is paid a value
    and the balance of an entity is the value
then it is not the case that the balance of the entity is the value.

it must not be true that
    a party is paid a value from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the balance of an entity is the value at the first time.

scenario one is:
    bob opens an escrow with miguel for 1600 from 0 to 1.
    bob deposits 1600 from 1 to 2.
    bob receives the goods from 4 to 5.
    bob rejects the goods from 6 to 7.
